IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 2526 of 2020
CITATION: (2023) 10 SCC 60
YEAR: 2023

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: S. Ravindra Bhat, Dipankar Datta

PARTIES:
PVVNL vs Raman Ispat Pvt Ltd

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016, Electricity Act, 2003

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 53 IBC, Section 238 IBC

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
waterfall mechanism, statutory dues vs secured creditors, override of other statutes

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that Section 53 waterfall mechanism under IBC prevails over recovery provisions under the Electricity Act, confirming the non-obstante priority of IBC under Section 238.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 53 IBC, Section 238 IBC.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

